course: dictionary
lesson: 12834
title: Places to stay
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An encampment is a place where a group of people sets up tents or shelters and stays for a time. «The soldiers built their encampment beside the river.» The word tells you that many people are living together in one place, using tents. Soldiers, refugees and travellers can all live in an encampment.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Refugees arrived at the encampment after the flood.» The sentence says refugees, which means people who have fled from danger, and the flood tells you why they needed shelter. Encampment must be a camp, a place to stay that is not a house.
explain: Test your idea by swapping in a simpler word. «The soldiers built their camp beside the river.» The sentence still makes sense, so camp is a good synonym. Encampment often sounds more formal, as in «a military encampment».
fact: An encampment is a place where a group sets up tents or shelters for a time.
fact: «Encampment» means a camp, especially a large or temporary one.
fact: Phrases to know: «a military encampment» (soldiers) and «a refugee encampment» (people who have fled).
fact: «The travellers' encampment was by the edge of the wood.» Here an encampment is a group of tents on the ground.
fact: The plural of encampment is encampments.
exercise: «The soldiers set up their encampment by the river.» What is an encampment? | *A place where a group sets up tents for a time | A kind of boat used on rivers | A large stone castle with tall walls | A deep hole dug in the ground
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as encampment? | Cave | *Camp | Castle | Canal
exercise: «Refugees arrived at the encampment after the flood.» Which group might live in a refugee encampment? | Cars parked on a motorway | *People who have fled from danger | Fish swimming in a river | Birds flying south for the winter
test: «The travellers' encampment was by the edge of the wood.» Where did the travellers stay? | A house with a garden | *In tents or shelters, in a camp | Under the sea | On a train
test: Which is most like a military encampment? | A busy shopping centre | *A group of tents where soldiers stay for weeks | A quiet library | A school playground
exam: Which sentence uses encampment correctly? | The encampment was a fast red car | She wrote an encampment on the page | I ate an encampment for my lunch | *The children built a small encampment of tents in the garden
